  "executive_briefing": "The digital asset landscape is undergoing a critical pivot marked by legislative friction, institutional maturation, and evolving cross-chain smart contract paradigms. The U.S. Digital Asset Market Clarity Act (H.R. 3633) faces intense Senate debate as merged text from the Banking and Agriculture committees encounters political gridlock over executive ethics provisions and holding exemptions. Institutionally, Bitcoin adoption has matured from initial spot ETF euphoria into structural balance sheet management, corporate treasury reserves, and structured bond vehicles. Concurrently, technical competition between Ethereum EVM dominance and Bitcoin native smart contracting via Clarity is accelerating, with trust-minimized cross-chain liquidity bridges enabling native BTC collateral to integrate directly with multi-chain DeFi ecosystems without centralized wrapper risk.",
